scalafim.phrfcmp.exec.SchedulePolicySuite:
  + dispatch is round-robin: index 0 of every cell, then index 1, in cell order 0.0s
  + probe wave is the first two datasets of every cell 0.001s
  + names that would escape the output tree are refused 0.001s
  + drop rule: D is the smallest per-cell count; higher indices dropped uniformly, highest first 0.001s
  + drop rule keeps the longest completed prefix: a hole is never kept, everything above it is dropped (D2) 0.0s
  + a resume must finish every incomplete job below the highest completed index, in any cell (D2) 0.001s
  + M2: a resume also finishes every dispatched incomplete job, at or above the highest completed index 0.0s
  + D < 15 refuses a partial pilot; D = 15 is accepted with df 14 0.001s
  + chi-square quantile and UCL factor are recomputed from df 0.0s
  + retries are capped at 2, refusals are never retried, done commits at once 0.001s
  + CPU guard: soft stop at 45 and hard stop at 60 core-hours, cumulative seconds 0.0s
  + ledger records are status only, carry invocation and run id, round-trip, and reject extra keys 0.001s
  + sealed names (F2): only the root check and the stamp are deterministic; every unit and aggregate name carries the run id 0.001s
  + stamp json is canonical and detects the first difference 0.001s
  + review 4: the hard ceiling is at most 60 core-hours unless the owner's typed authorization raises it 0.001s
  + re-review 6: OwnerCeilingRaise and OwnerAccountingRecovery hold their invariants; no generated constructor bypasses them 0.003s
scalafim.phrfcmp.exec.PilotAggregationSuite:
  + the aggregator runs in-process; its sealed diagnostics and record are appended to the sealed store and nowhere else 0.85s
  + the aggregate takes the runner's run id: scorer inputs of another invocation are refused 0.052s
  + a closed store refuses the append with a typed seal error 0.273s
  + once per run id: a second aggregation with the same run id is refused before anything is sealed, even with another corpus 0.723s
  + corpus digests: the outcome digest depends on the corpus content and not on the run; timing is digested separately 0.329s
  + R5 (M1): aggregating a partial pilot and later the full one in the same store leaves a store the owner reads 0.508s
  + F4: end to end, the aggregate record localises a nondeterministic unit; a deterministic pilot has no deviation 2.966s
scalafim.phrfcmp.exec.SealedStoreSuite:
  + append seals every blob; file name is the hash of the whole file; reader recovers names and data 0.038s
  + nothing result-bearing reaches disk in plaintext, including temp files 0.036s
  + read-back: a corrupted ciphertext is refused and nothing is published 0.001s
  + read-back: a blob that decrypts to different plaintext is refused 0.002s
  + read-back from disk: a file that differs after the durable write is removed and refused 0.013s
  + crash between tmp write and rename leaves only ciphertext tmp debris; readers and digest ignore it; close deletes it 0.053s
  + resume re-seals: identical duplicates are accepted, differing duplicates are refused by the reader 0.093s
  + close: CLOSE counts every data-blob file, SEALED receipt matches the digest, a second close and later appends refuse 0.057s
  + a wrong fingerprint refuses before any byte is written 0.0s
  + size buckets: ciphertext length reveals only the bucket 0.055s
  + sealed-tree digest is sensitive to one byte and excludes SEALED and tmp files 0.011s
  + concurrent appends from many threads all verify and unseal 0.891s
